export anchor WrittenBriefStyle:
    number: 194
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Written brief
    idea: The dashboard opens with a short written paragraph that states the week in plain sentences, then hands over to one carefully set sortable table, like a briefing memo from a good analyst.
    base: light
    palette:
        paper: #faf8f4, the page behind the brief
        surface: #ffffff, the top bar, the table body, fields and the style sheet
        ink: #1d232b, text, progress fills and the 2px section rules
        slate: #535d6a, meta, notes and axis labels
        rule: #ddd7cc, hairlines between rows, never text
        ruleStrong: #8c8477, the table header rule, field borders and last week bars
        teal: #0d5c63, the primary button, the sorted column, this week bars and focus
        tealTint: #e4efee, the focused or selected table row
        green: #1b6b3a, On track with a solid dot
        amber: #8a5100, At risk with a solid triangle
        red: #a8261f, Behind with a solid square and the overdue phrase
        redTint: #f8e6e3, the highlight behind the overdue phrase
    type:
        Two stacks. Prose and headings use Charter, Bitstream Charter,
        Iowan Old Style, Sitka Text, Cambria, Georgia, serif. Interface text
        uses system-ui, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting
        is 34px serif regular, the summary paragraph 21px serif at 1.6 with
        figures in bold, fact figures 22px sans semibold tabular, table text
        14px, and section labels 12 to 13px semibold caps tracked 0.08em.
    layout:
        A white top bar holds a square outline mark with the serif brand,
        six text nav links with a 2px teal underline on Home, then a search
        field, a teal New project button, a square bell and initials with
        Mara Okafor. Content sits in one centred 1040px column. A caps
        dateline and the serif greeting lead into a written paragraph that
        opens with a red tinted clock phrase for the 4 overdue tasks and
        names totals and the two troubled projects in sentences. Under it a
        ruled facts line shows the four summary numbers inline, split by
        thin vertical rules. The table follows with a caps heading, a note
        that it is sorted by due date, and a segmented filter of All 6,
        Needs attention 2 and On track 4. Columns are Project with team,
        Status, Progress as a thin ink bar with percent, Tasks done, Due and
        Days left, with sort buttons in a warm header row and Due marked
        ascending. Troubled rows carry a 3px red or amber inset edge and a
        footer row totals 78 of 170. Below, a 5 to 7 split puts a paired bar
        chart of last week and this week by weekday beside an activity list
        with times in a left column, each topped by a 2px ink rule. Below
        1000px the nav moves to its own scrolling row and the lower band
        stacks. On phones table rows become ruled cards with name and
        status on top, the bar, then tasks, due and days left.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px cell padding and 40 to 48px between the brief, the table and the lower band.
    density: Medium. Prose and facts carry the headline and one table carries the detail.
    corners: Nearly square. 3px on controls and nothing on the table, tracks or swatches.
    borders: Warm 1px hairlines between rows, a stronger rule under the table header and a 2px ink rule over the chart and activity.
    shadows: None. Depth comes only from paper against white.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.6px and 18px for search, bell, plus and sort
        arrows. Status uses small solid shapes beside the word, a dot for
        On track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind, and the
        overdue phrase carries a clock.
    focus: A solid 2px teal outline offset 2px, and a teal tint plus outline on a focused table row.
    tone: Full sentences in the brief and short nouns in the table, such as Days left and Needs attention 2.
